The present work explores a smaller command vocabulary using inexpensive hardware. The system
recognizes Neutral, Up, Down, and Blink states from vertical EOG recordings and maps those states to a
basic computer-control interface.
The main objectives of the study are:
2
1. to implement vertical EOG acquisition using a BioAmp EXG Pill and ESP32;
2. to collect a balanced four-class EOG dataset;
3. to represent each recorded trial using 28 engineered signal features;
4. to compare Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, and RBF-SVM classifiers;
5. to evaluate performance at trial level rather than relying only on overlapping windows; and
6. to integrate the trained model into a real-time cursor-control prototype.
